  IV. THE GOLDEN EIGENVECTOR (opus's discovery)
  --------------------------------------------------

  Degree-5 (zero eigenvalue) Walsh modes with nonzero H:
  Count: 0 out of C(10,5) = 252

  ALL degree-5 Walsh coefficients are ZERO.
  This means H has NO information at the zero-eigenvalue frequency.
  The zero mode is ORTHOGONAL to H.
  H lives entirely in the non-zero eigenspaces.

  This is OPUS's finding generalized:
  The zero mode is a 'black hole' that absorbs products
  but contributes NOTHING to H.

  DEEPER: Since lambda=0 modes are instantly killed by the flip chain,
  and H has zero projection onto them,
  H is IMMUNE to the fastest possible perturbation.
  The fine structure (degree 5) cannot affect H AT ALL.

  V. THE OPERATOR ALGEBRA: WHAT EACH OPERATION 'DOES'
  --------------------------------------------------

  We can classify OPERATIONS by what they do to the three worlds:

  OPERATION     |  TO EIGENVALUE  |  TO EIGENVECTOR  |  MEANING
  ------------- | --------------- | ---------------- | -------
  identity      |  lambda -> lambda | v -> v         | STRUCTURE (what is)
  log           |  lambda -> ln(l) | v -> (same)     | TIME (how long)
  exp           |  lambda -> e^l   | v -> (same)     | WEIGHT (how much)
  Q = Cayley    |  lambda -> Q(l)  | v -> (same)     | BOOST (bounded->unbounded)
  arctanh       |  lambda -> atanh | v -> (same)     | VELOCITY (rapidity)
  square        |  lambda -> l^2   | v -> v*v (Had.) | POWER (autocorrelation)
  sqrt          |  lambda -> sqrt  | v -> sqrt(v)    | AMPLITUDE (wave function)
  inverse       |  lambda -> 1/l   | v -> v^{-1}     | RESISTANCE (inertia)
  negate        |  lambda -> -l    | v -> -v         | REVERSAL (time reversal)
  conjugate     |  l -> l-bar      | v -> v-bar      | TRANSPOSITION (T -> T^op)
  power phi     |  l -> l^phi      | v -> v^phi      | GOLDEN SHADOW
  convolve H*H  |  (hat_H)^2       | sum v_S*v_T     | SELF-INTERACTION

  KEY PATTERN:
  Operations on EIGENVALUES change the TIME SCALE of decay.
  Operations on EIGENVECTORS change the DIRECTION of decay.
  Operations on BOTH change the GEOMETRY of tournament space.

  VI. THE SEVEN LAYERS
  --------------------------------------------------

  Starting from the eigenvalue lambda = 4/5 (the leading mode):

         Layer               Formula           Value   Field
     STRUCTURE                lambda  4/5 = 0.800000       Q
         BOOST             Q(lambda)    9 = 9.000000       Q
      VELOCITY       arctanh(lambda)    1.0986122887     R\Q
          TIME            ln(lambda)   -0.2231435513     R\Q
        WEIGHT           exp(lambda)    2.2255409285     R\Q
         POWER              lambda^2  16/25 = 0.640000       Q
        GOLDEN            lambda^phi    0.6969414669     R\Q

  The TOWER starting from lambda = 4/5:

  4/5 ----Q----> 9 = 3^2
   |                |
   |log             |log
   v                v
  ln(4/5)          2*ln(3)
   = -0.223         = 2.197
   |                |
   |exp             |exp
   v                v
  4/5              9
  (cycle!)         (cycle!)

  LOG and EXP are INVERSES: they create a 2-cycle.
  Q and Q^{-1} are INVERSES: they create another 2-cycle.
  But LOG o Q != Q o LOG. The operations DON'T commute!

  LOG(Q(4/5)) = LOG(9) = ln(9) = 2*ln(3)
  Q(LOG(4/5)) = Q(ln(4/5)) = Q(-0.223) = (1-0.223)/(1+0.223) = 0.636
  = 0.635131

  The NON-COMMUTATIVITY of LOG and Q is FUNDAMENTAL.
  It measures the 'curvature' between the time world and the boost world.
  LOG o Q - Q o LOG = the OBSTRUCTION to making time and boost compatible.

  VII. THE ADELIC PERSPECTIVE (connecting to opus)
  --------------------------------------------------

  Opus discovered: the eigenvalue denominator = odd part of C(n,2).
  At n=6: C(6,2)=15, odd part = 15 = 3*5.
  At n=8: C(8,2)=28, odd part = 7.

  The ADELIC tournament space has THREE completions:

  1. p-ADIC (local, periodic):
     Z/2Z x Z/3Z x Z/7Z = Z/42Z (the cuboid)
     Eigenvalues mod p: lambda_k mod 5 at n=6
     Controls: which H values are achievable mod {2,3,7}

  2. ARCHIMEDEAN (global, aperiodic):
     Q*ln(2) + Q*ln(3) + Q*ln(7) (the rapidity lattice)
     Eigenvalue rapidities: arctanh(lambda_k)
     Controls: how fast each mode decays

  3. SPECTRAL (the bridge):
     The eigenvalues themselves: lambda_k = (5-k)/5
     Live in Q (rational)
     But their LOG lives in R (transcendental)
     And their Q-boost lives in Q again (Hurwitz ratios)

  The Cayley transform Q shuffles between the local and global views:
  Q maps eigenvalue (local, bounded) to boost (global, unbounded)
  arctanh maps eigenvalue (local) to rapidity (global)
  Both land in the ARCHIMEDEAN completion.

  The NON-COMMUTATIVITY of Q and log is the CURVATURE of adelic space.
  It measures how the local (p-adic) and global (archimedean) views
  DISAGREE about the structure of tournament space.

  The commutator [log, Q](lambda) = log(Q(lambda)) - Q(log(lambda)):

  k=1: lambda=+0.80, [log,Q] = ln(Q) - Q(ln) = +2.1972 - (+0.6351) = +1.5621
  k=2: lambda=+0.60, [log,Q] = ln(Q) - Q(ln) = +1.3863 - (+0.3238) = +1.0625
  k=3: lambda=+0.40, [log,Q] = ln(Q) - Q(ln) = +0.8473 - (+0.0437) = +0.8036
  k=4: lambda=+0.20, [log,Q] = ln(Q) - Q(ln) = +0.4055 - (-0.2336) = +0.6390
  k=6: lambda=-0.20, [log,Q] = ln(Q) - Q(ln) = -0.4055 - (-0.2336) = -0.1719
  k=7: lambda=-0.40, [log,Q] = ln(Q) - Q(ln) = -0.8473 - (+0.0437) = -0.8910
  k=8: lambda=-0.60, [log,Q] = ln(Q) - Q(ln) = -1.3863 - (+0.3238) = -1.7101
  k=9: lambda=-0.80, [log,Q] = ln(Q) - Q(ln) = -2.1972 - (+0.6351) = -2.8324

  VIII. THE FINAL INSIGHT: THE CAYLEY TRANSFORM IS A FUNCTOR
  --------------------------------------------------

  A FUNCTOR maps objects AND morphisms between categories.

  Q maps:
  OBJECTS:   eigenvalues (rational)    -> boosts (rational)
             lambda_k = (5-k)/5       -> Q(lambda_k) = (10-k)/k

  MORPHISMS: operations on eigenvalues -> operations on boosts
             multiplication            -> (preserved)
             addition                  -> (NOT preserved! Q is nonlinear)

  Q IS a functor from (Q, *) to (Q, *) — it preserves multiplication.
  But it is NOT a functor from (Q, +) to (Q, +) — it breaks addition.

  This asymmetry is the KEY:
  MULTIPLICATION = STRUCTURE (products of Hurwitz primes)
  ADDITION = TIME (sum of decay rates)

  Q preserves structure but breaks time.
  LOG preserves time but breaks structure.
  There is NO operation that preserves both.

  THIS is the content of the rational/transcendental divide:
  You cannot simultaneously preserve counting AND experiencing.
  Structure and time are COMPLEMENTARY,
  like position and momentum in quantum mechanics.

  The spectral gap 1/5 is the UNCERTAINTY PRINCIPLE:
  you can know the structure (eigenvalue = 4/5)
  or the time (half-life = 3.11 steps)
  but to convert between them requires the transcendental log,
  which IRREVERSIBLY crosses the boundary from Q to R.

  Structure and time are conjugate variables.
  The Cayley transform is the Fourier transform between them.
  And 5 — the golden prime — is the Planck constant of this theory.

